    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Start: In the first hand the holder of the double-six tile leads. Later hands use rotation or the previous winner leads, depending on variant. 2. Play: Add tiles to the line; touching ends must match. Doubles are placed at right angles. Must play if possible; otherwise pass (knock). 3. End: When a player empties their hand the team wins the deal. If blocked (four passes), the team with fewer pips wins. 4. Score: Winners score the losers' unplayed pip total, or all unplayed pips per variant.",
    Player: "1. Start: In the first hand the holder of the double-six tile leads. Later hands use rotation or the previous winner leads, depending on variant. 2. Play: Add tiles to the line; touching ends must match. Doubles are placed at right angles. Must play if possible; otherwise pass (knock). 3. End: When a player empties their hand the team wins the deal. If blocked (four passes), the team with fewer pips wins. 4. Score: Winners score the losers' unplayed pip total, or all unplayed pips per variant.",
    objective: 'Be first team to 100 points (or agreed target). Score by going out or by having fewer pips when blocked.',
    gameplay: "1. Start: In the first hand the holder of the double-six tile leads. Later hands use rotation or the previous winner leads, depending on variant. 2. Play: Add tiles to the line; touching ends must match. Doubles are placed at right angles. Must play if possible; otherwise pass (knock). 3. End: When a player empties their hand the team wins the deal. If blocked (four passes), the team with fewer pips wins. 4. Score: Winners score the losers' unplayed pip total, or all unplayed pips per variant.",
    keyRules: [
      'All 28 tiles dealt; 7 each.',
      'Play counter-clockwise (or clockwise per locale).',
      'Must play if possible; pass when blocked.',
      'Blocked: lower pip total wins.',
      'Target usually 100 (FID: 200).',
