      'Setup example: 7 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be first team to 100 points (or agreed target). Score by going out or by having fewer pips when blocked.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. Start: In the first hand the holder of the double-six tile leads. Later hands use rotation or the previous winner leads, depending on variant. 2. Play: Add tiles to the line; touching ends must match. Doubles are placed at right angles. Must play if possible; otherwise pass (knock). 3. End: When a player empties their hand the team wins the deal. If blocked (four passes), the team with fewer pips wins. 4. Score: Winners score the losers' unplayed pip total, or all unplayed pips per variant.",
      "Scoring example: Winners score losers' unplayed pips. Blocked: lower pip total wins. Tie = no score (or variant rules). First team to 100 (or 200) cumulative points..",
